When an event handler updates data that affects the UI, let **computed properties** handle derived state. This keeps your methods focused and your reactivity predictable.

```javascript
methods: {
  addItem() {
    this.items.push({ text: this.newItem });
    this.newItem = '';
  }
},
computed: {
  itemCount() {
    return this.items.length;
  }
}
```

For events that fire rapidly (like `@input` or `@scroll`), consider **debouncing** or **throttling** to avoid performance issues.

```html
<input @input="debouncedSearch">
```

```javascript
methods: {
  debouncedSearch: _.debounce(function() {
    // search logic
  }, 300)
}
```

Libraries like Lodash provide these utilities.
